      "relevant": false,
      "not_relevant_because": "The one manuscript, 'Positive lower density of large prime gaps', proves that for each fixed C > 0 a positive proportion of indices n up to N have p_{n+1} - p_n > C log p_n. The gaps it counts grow without bound with p, so beyond some point they can never equal a fixed even n. The result therefore says nothing about whether any fixed even n occurs as a prime gap infinitely often, which is what Polignac's conjecture asks.",
